  "deliberate_differences": [
    "Env reads are constants with 1007804's values (see constants and features). The copied kernels/fp4_mla_packed_reduce.py answers TRTLLM_FP4_MLA_REDUCE_SPREAD_STATS / REDUCE_PDL / F16_PARTIALS with 1007804's \"1\" (constants); the glue passes reduce_pdl / f16_partials explicitly, and spread_stats is only read by the standalone reduction, which the deferred fused tail does not launch.",
    "The served backend dispatch (MLA.forward -> TrtllmAttention.forward -> FP4 / FMHA backend objects, autotuner custom op) is unrolled into explicit calls: FP4 layers call ops/attention/k3_fp4_mla_decode, FP8 layers call ops/attention/k3_mla_decode_fp8 with the served runner's default tactic. Paths the deployment does not reach (non-Helix GEN, no-FP8 non-FP4 KV, layer.mqa.forward fallback) raise instead of falling back.",
    "The FP4 RoPE + KV append launches the served _fp4_mla_generation_fused_qk_rope_cache_update_kernel (copied file) through the served glue; the old renamed copy kernels/fp4_mla_kv_append.py and the extra plan launch it made are gone. Plan, lengths and page table come from the step state (_fp4_mla_decode) as in served, one launch per step.",
    "forward_gen_q_fused does not allocate the q_input / q_pe buffers served allocates and never reads (no kernels either way).",
    "Workspace attribute names on the metadata keep the _k3_* prefix; the FP8 split plan keeps served's _cute_dsl_mla_split_plan / _key names.",
    "The identity-RoPE table is installed by mla.py's own helper (same values as served _write_identity_rope_values).",
    "FP8-KV layer selection is the engine's (kimi_k3_cache_policy) and raises for a full NVFP4 model whose selection is not {91, 92}, instead of trusting a hard-coded set.",
    "TRTLLM_MNNVL_AR_ONESHOT_MAX_BYTES=2097152 governs the o_proj allreduce one-shot threshold in served; that lives in the layers / distributed area, not here.",
    "MLAIN: served shadows mixer._project_qkv_a and g_proj.forward_sigmoid for the call; here K3MLARuntime.decode_attention consumes `released` and, where takes_q_fused holds, hands it to the mixer as mlain_released, which project_qkv_a reads (the same fold_call / forward_mxfp8(stage_weights=True) / BF16 choice) and _gate_of returns the folded gate for the same input object. Served's MlaInAttention wraps only layers that serve MLAIN (_serves, rows <= 16, UllConfig.mlain); takes_q_fused implies an FP4-KV gated layer of <= 16 rows, and with no MXFP8 rows handed over the MLAIN projection is the module projection, so the result is the same.",
    "MLAIN: no forward-hook fallback (served MlaAttention.fallback): the target registers no forward hooks.",
    "MLAIN: the fold is also built eagerly in build_chain (prepare_in_fold, outside capture) besides served's build on first use; mlain_fold keeps served's is_current rebuild. FoldedInProj.build returns None where a projection has no packed_weight_scale (served would raise AttributeError there; the deployment's FP8 projections have it)."
